DTSTAMP:20260621T050056Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260621T120000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260621T140000
SUMMARY:With Strength: Toronto Women on the Edge of History!
DESCRIPTION:Toronto History Walks\n\\*\\***The Toronto History Walks Yearl
 y Pass is available. Get it now for $125.00 for 1 year of unlimited tours\
 , email**\n**torontohistorywalks@gmail.com**\n**for more information or fo
 r signing up!\\*\\***\n\n\\*\\* **Please note: Please e-transfer the ticke
 t amount when booking your space for this tour! You can e-transfer to the 
 following email at:**\n**torontohistorywalks@gmail.com**\n\nThis tour debu
 ted on September 5\, 2020! Five years of storytelling!\n\nToronto is a cit
 y of stories.\n\nIt's also a city constantly reinventing and learning abou
 t itself. It has been for the last 300 years. The people of Toronto are th
 e storytellers\, and throughout its history\, women have been at the foref
 ront of change.\n\nLike Elizabeth Neufeld\, Hester How\, Mary Pickford\, o
 r Clara Martin stories that have shaped Toronto. Stories that have shaped 
 the lives of people in Toronto today.\n\nExplore the lives of ordinary wom
 en of Toronto who have made extraordinary impacts on our lives. From the d
 eath and destruction of war to the magic of Hollywood\, these women create
 d their own endings. But for many in our city today these names and many o
 thers are forgotten\, their accomplishments dusted over and buried in the 
 mists of time\, but not for long. These courageous Torontonians created on
 e lasting story to be told: Their story!\n\nToronto is a city of meaning a
 nd hidden stories indeed. Mary Pickford\, the first great screen Hollywood
  star looks into the camera above. Born on University Avenue near College 
 Street\, she rewrote the Hollywood story and put Toronto on the film map.\
 n\nThis walk is for all fitness levels.\n\nThe meeting place for this impo
 rtant walking adventure is the Barbara Ann Scott Ice Trail behind College 
 Park at the southwest corner of Yonge Street and College Street. We end ou
 r walk at the park adjacent to St. Lawrence Hall.\n\nThis tour has a ticke
 t price of $15.00 per person!\n\n\\*\\* **Please note: Please e-transfer t
 he ticket amount when booking your space for this tour! You can e-transfer
  to the following email at:**\n**torontohistorywalks@gmail.com**
URL;VALUE=URI:https://www.meetup.com/the-history-of-parkdale/events/314641
 143/
STATUS:CONFIRMED
CREATED:20260505T122308Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260505T122308Z
CLASS:PUBLIC
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:Meetup: History of Parkdale
UID:event_314641089@meetup.com
SEQUENCE:1
DTSTAMP:20260621T050056Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260621T153000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260621T173000
SUMMARY:Trio of Evil  (Mercer Reformatory\, Central Prison and the Lunatic
  Asylum) 
DESCRIPTION:Toronto History Walks\n\\*\\***The Toronto History Walks Explo
 rer Pass is available. Get it now for $125.00 for 1 year of unlimited tour
 s\, email**\n**torontohistorywalks@gmail.com**\n**for more information or 
 for signing up!\\*\\***\n\n\\*\\* **Please note: Please e-transfer the tic
 ket price when booking your space for this tour! You can e-transfer to the
  following email at:**\n**torontohistorywalks@gmail.com**\n\nA shocking st
 ory from the Toronto history books.\n\nMercer\, the Central Prison\, and t
 he Asylum all had stories of abuse of the patients and inmates. Once a per
 son was locked behind the doors of these institutions they were forgotten 
 and shunned. A part of shameful Toronto history.\n\nBut the history has no
 t been shared with Torontonians willingly. The stories are now just emergi
 ng. And these stories will shock walkers. This extensive tour shines a lig
 ht on the inner workings of these three institutions. We will concentrate 
 on the history of these three\, the history and buildings that have surviv
 ed to this day\, and how to tell these stories going forward!\n\nWhat went
  on behind closed doors would shock even the most shock proof of individua
 ls. Travel back to the time of the Mercer\, the Central Prison\, and the P
 rovincial Lunatic Asylum! All three within a square mile in west end Toron
 to. A coincidence\, I think not!\n\nThe tour begins at the northeast corne
 r of Fraser Avenue & King Street West just two blocks east of Dufferin Str
 eet on King Street.\n\nThis tour has a ticket price of $15.00 per person!\
 n\n\\*\\* **Please note: Please e-transfer the ticket price when booking y
 our space for this tour! You can e-transfer to the following email at:**\n
 **torontohistorywalks@gmail.com**
URL;VALUE=URI:https://www.meetup.com/the-history-of-parkdale/events/314641
 089/
STATUS:CONFIRMED
CREATED:20260505T121503Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260505T121503Z
CLASS:PUBLIC
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:Meetup: History of Parkdale
UID:event_314641182@meetup.com
SEQUENCE:1
DTSTAMP:20260621T050056Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260627T120000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260627T140000
SUMMARY:The PATH System: Specialist Course and Guide! (FULL PATH TOUR)
DESCRIPTION:Toronto History Walks\n\\*\\***The Toronto History Walks Yearl
 y Pass is available. Get it now for $125.00 for 1 year of unlimited tours\
 , email**\n**torontohistorywalks@gmail.com**\n**for more information or fo
 r signing up!\\*\\***\n\n\\*\\* **Please note: Please e-transfer the ticke
 t amount when booking your space for this tour! You can e-transfer to the 
 following email at:**\n**torontohistorywalks@gmail.com**\n\nSo many walker
 s have expressed interest in a full explanation of the dreaded PATH\, so h
 ere it is. A full course on the PATH\, its history and explanation. You wi
 ll become a PATH specialist after this\, guaranteed!\n\nI've heard it so m
 any times\, with so many people\, the common refrain\, "I got lost in the 
 PATH." If you are one of the many who have simply vanished in Toronto's un
 derground never to be seen again\, check out this popular historical walki
 ng tour.\n\nThis tour demystifies the PATH system and explains how it work
 s in grand detail. It takes walkers through the system and points out the 
 crucial connectors and branches within the system to effortlessly guide th
 e lost through the maze. Once experienced the PATH will be an invaluable a
 id to navigating the downtown\, in both summer and winter\, rain or shine\
 , hurricane or drought. You might even enjoy getting lost in the undergrou
 nd\, lost but not forgotten.\n\nThis is the full PATH course curriculum:\n
 \nPart 1: The History of THE PATH\nPart2: Connectors and signboards\nPart 
 3: Understanding the above ground connection\nPart 4: Hidden paths to get 
 one around quickly\nPart 5: The Blind Spots and how to work with them\nPar
 t 6: The Maps\nPart 7: Getting from here to there!\n\nThis walk is for all
  fitness levels and skills. This tour is indoors\, so please dress for the
  conditions\, and is considered an all-weather​ tour.\n\nThe walk begins
  **inside** the Atrium on Bay at the northeast corner of Dundas Street Wes
 t and Bay Street adjacent to the Red Lobster restaurant!\n\nThis tour has 
 a ticket price of $15.00 per person!\n\n\\*\\* **Please note: Please e-tra
 nsfer the ticket amount when booking your space for this tour! You can e-t
 ransfer to the following email at:**\n**torontohistorywalks@gmail.com**
URL;VALUE=URI:https://www.meetup.com/the-history-of-parkdale/events/314641
 182/
STATUS:CONFIRMED
CREATED:20260505T122832Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260505T122832Z
CLASS:PUBLIC
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:Meetup: History of Parkdale
UID:event_314641111@meetup.com
SEQUENCE:1
DTSTAMP:20260621T050056Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260628T110000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260628T130000
SUMMARY:Historic Little India: Gerrard India Bazaar (REVISED FOR 2026)
DESCRIPTION:Toronto History Walks\n\\*\\***The Toronto History Walks Explo
 rer Pass is available. Get it now for $125.00 for 1 year of unlimited tour
 s\, email**\n**torontohistorywalks@gmail.com**\n**for more information or 
 for signing up!\\*\\***\n\n\\*\\* **Please note: Please e-transfer the Tic
 ket amount when booking your space for this tour! You can e-transfer to th
 e following email at:**\n**torontohistorywalks@gmail.com**\n\nThe story of
  historic Little India is a true Toronto success story\, a unique look at 
 a neighbourhood and the people who call it home. But the story is not alwa
 ys a happy one. Like all other areas in Toronto\, Little India started out
  as a purely English - Anglican area and was repeatedly changed as other i
 mmigrants opted to leave the security of the downtown core for outer areas
 .\n\nWith the opening of the Naaz theatre in 1972\, the community that bec
 ame Little India started to take shape\, but in Toronto the forces that de
 veloped communities were different in that part of the city sandwiched bet
 ween Leslieville to the south\, and Greektown to the north.\n\nWith a stri
 ctly Anglo-Saxon pro-British community entrenched for over 100 years\, now
  changing to include south Asians\, the area was seen as a rather depresse
 d area\, or an area in transition\, and violence was an unfortunate part o
 f life. Racial tensions increased dramatically with the influx of south As
 ians.\n\nBut by the 1980s and 1990s the district had found its feet\, and 
 Little India was a popular Toronto district and tourist attraction\, with 
 visitors pouring in from around the world to partake of the richness. A tr
 ue cultural enclave in Toronto! A fascinating history and a fascinating co
 mmunity awaits! This tour has been revised a few times to add more histori
 c information to the walk\, it has been revised once again for 2026 with n
 ew landmarks and stories attached. Should be a fascinating walk!\n\nThis w
 alk is for all fitness levels. The meeting place for our walking adventure
  is on the southwest corner of Greenwood Avenue and Gerrard Street East!\n
 \nThis tour has a ticket price of $15.00 per person!\n\n\\*\\* **Please no
 te: Please e-transfer the Ticket amount when booking your space for this t
 our! You can e-transfer to the following email at:**\n**torontohistorywalk
 s@gmail.com**
URL;VALUE=URI:https://www.meetup.com/the-history-of-parkdale/events/314641
 111/
STATUS:CONFIRMED
CREATED:20260505T121801Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260505T121801Z
CLASS:PUBLIC
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:Meetup: History of Parkdale
UID:event_314890249@meetup.com
SEQUENCE:1
DTSTAMP:20260621T050056Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260704T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260704T160000
SUMMARY:University of Toronto and Historic Yorkville!
DESCRIPTION:Toronto History Walks\n\\*\\***The Toronto History Walks Explo
 rer Pass is available. Get it now for $125.00 for 1 year of unlimited tour
 s\, email**\n**torontohistorywalks@gmail.com**\n**for more information or 
 for signing up!\\*\\***\n\n\\*\\* **Please note: Please e-transfer the tic
 ket price when booking your space for this tour! You can e-transfer to the
  following email at:**\n**torontohistorywalks@gmail.com**\n\nGet your hist
 ory fix with this special double tour. It combines both U of T and histori
 c Yorkville in one shot.\n\nOn March 15\, 1827\, a royal charter was issue
 d by King George IV\, for the establishment of King's College. The charter
  was the result of the efforts of John Strachan\, the Anglican Bishop of T
 oronto\, the College's first president.\n\nKing's College was a religious 
 institution tied to the Church of England and the Family Compact. In 1849\
 , the newly elected government of Canada voted to rename the College\, Uni
 versity of Toronto and broke with the church. Strachan resigned to open Tr
 inity College as a private seminary.\n\nUniversity College was created as 
 a branch of University of Toronto. During the American Civil War\, the thr
 eat of Union blockade prompted the creation of the University Rifle Corps\
 , which saw action against the Fenians on the Niagara border in 1866.\n\nF
 ounded in 1830 by Joseph Bloor\, and William Botsford Jarvis\, the Village
  of Yorkville was muddy York's northern residential suburb.\n\nWith histor
 ic establishments like The Red Lion Inn\, Yorkville Town Hall or even the 
 fierce political radical William Lyon Mackenzie\, it was here that notorie
 ty was achieved\, in Yorkville itself.\n\nOmnibus horse drawn streetcar se
 rvice started in 1849 to connect the old St. Lawrence Market in Toronto wi
 th Yorkville\, and by 1853\, the population of the village had reached 1\,
 000 residents.\n\nBy the 1870s\, Potter's Field\, a cemetery stretching we
 st of Yonge Street at Bloor Street was closed\, and the remains moved to o
 ther area cemeteries. Yorkville was growing fast\, and soon Toronto was re
 ady to pull the neighbourhood into its orbit. On February 1\, 1883\, Yorkv
 ille's name changed officially. It was now known as St. Paul's Ward!\n\nTh
 is walking tour is for all fitness levels and skills. Please dress for the
  weather. The extensive walking tour begins at the Queen's Park SUBWAY Sta
 tion at the **southwest corner** of University Avenue and College Street a
 djacent to the Tim Horton's at the corner.\n\nThe walk ends at the Toronto
  Reference Library at Yonge Street and Asquith.\n\nThis tour has a ticket 
 price of $15.00 per person!\n\n\\*\\* **Please note: Please e-transfer the
  ticket price when booking your space for this tour! You can e-transfer to
  the following email at:**\n**torontohistorywalks@gmail.com**
URL;VALUE=URI:https://www.meetup.com/the-history-of-parkdale/events/314890
 249/
STATUS:CONFIRMED
CREATED:20260521T121514Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260521T121514Z
CLASS:PUBLIC
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:Meetup: History of Parkdale
UID:event_314890106@meetup.com
SEQUENCE:1
DTSTAMP:20260621T050056Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260705T120000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260705T150000
SUMMARY:The Massey Murder: Interactive Game and Tour!
DESCRIPTION:Toronto History Walks\n\\*\\***The Toronto History Walks Explo
 rer Pass is available. Get it now for $125.00 for 1 year of unlimited tour
 s\, email**\n**torontohistorywalks@gmail.com**\n**for more information or 
 for signing up!\\*\\***\n\n\\*\\* **Please note: Please e-transfer the tic
 ket amount when booking your space for this tour! You can e-transfer to th
 e following email at:**\n**torontohistorywalks@gmail.com**\n\nFirst it was
  **Ambrose Small** and my team of brilliant detectives who tried to figure
  it all out. The walkers on this tour just about cracked the case. Well do
 ne my detectives. But your smarts are needed again however. The Harley Kar
 ulis Detective Agency needs your help!\n\nThe famous murder of Burt Massey
  on Walmer Road awaits your inspection. This time we are needed as **juror
 s** to figure the case out and add a fresh perspective. Are you up for thi
 s interactive game once again?\n\nThe story shocked the city back in Febru
 ary of 1915.\n\nHow a young teenage maid shot and killed her boss on Walme
 r Road in the Annex made headlines across Canada and around the world. But
  it was the name of that boss that made people gasp\, the Massey family\, 
 from the famous music hall of the same name on Shuter Street in downtown T
 oronto! And people talked and tried to come up with explanations.\n\nBut t
 he following trial exposed the undercurrents of Toronto life\, and the cla
 ss system that was in place. This trial changed Toronto at a crucial time 
 in its history. The first World War was raging in Europe\, and residents o
 f the city now had something else to think about.\n\nMurder!\n\nHow this c
 ould have happened to an upper middle class family in the centre of Toront
 o\, the Annex neighbourhood was rife with theory and fears.\n\nThis walkin
 g tour/game takes participants back in time to the 1915 trial and explores
  the many sites associated with the trial and the personalities involved. 
 You will be introduced to 15 historic characters and each has their own da
 rk secrets\, it will be up to you to render a **verdict** in this case. Gu
 ilty\, or Not Guilty\, and was the trial fair\, those are the questions th
 at need answering! Are you up for it?\n\nSites like the National Club and 
 the Toronto Club\, Old City Hall and the Morgue are explored and their sto
 ries exposed.\n\n**This tour requires a PRESTO card for TTC as this tour u
 ses transit to get around the city for stops outside the downtown core. On
 e could call it a hop on hop off walking tour!**\n\nOur walk begins on the
  steps of Old City Hall at the northeast corner of Bay Street and Queen St
 reet West. We end the tour at the site of the murder in the Annex for the 
 reading of the verdict! Just like in the Ambrose Small case\, we end where
  it all begins!\n\nThis tour has a ticket price of $15.00 per person. Plea
 se get your tickets early if you would like to attend.\n\n\\*\\* **Please 
 note: Please e-transfer the ticket price when booking your space for this 
 tour! You can e-transfer to the following email at:**\n**torontohistorywal
 ks@gmail.com**
URL;VALUE=URI:https://www.meetup.com/the-history-of-parkdale/events/314890
 106/
STATUS:CONFIRMED
CREATED:20260521T121020Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260521T121020Z
CLASS:PUBLIC
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:Meetup: History of Parkdale
UID:event_314890300@meetup.com
SEQUENCE:1
DTSTAMP:20260621T050056Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260711T120000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260711T140000
SUMMARY:Leslieville!
DESCRIPTION:Toronto History Walks\n\\*\\***The Toronto History Walks Yearl
 y Pass is available. Get it now for $125.00 for 1 year of unlimited tours\
 , email**\n**torontohistorywalks@gmail.com**\n**for more information or fo
 r signing up!\\*\\***\n\n\\*\\* **Please note: Please e-transfer the ticke
 t price when booking your space for this tour! You can e-transfer to the f
 ollowing email at:**\n**torontohistorywalks@gmail.com**\n\nLeslieville was
  established in the 1850s\, by George Leslie (1804-1893).\n\nMajority of t
 he early residents were gardeners or brick makers at one of the many brick
 -making factories in the area. This was an industrial area on the edge of 
 Toronto. Leslie's original home at Queen Street East and Leslie Street was
  demolished years ago\, but plenty of history remains for the interested w
 alker!\n\nSouth Riverdale as Leslieville is sometimes called was home to l
 ight industry. Eastern Ave. south of Queen Street East. hosted both metal 
 processing and tanning businesses. However\, with that type of industry ca
 me the dangers of contaminated land. Leslieville has been dealing with tha
 t problem for decades.\n\nAlmost all of these industrial areas have been a
 bandoned and are being redeveloped as prime residential areas.\n\nAnd let'
 s not forget Alexander Muir. And we all know about him\, and his daydreami
 ng under a maple tree and what that led to? Hope to see you on this fascin
 ating walking tour. A great start to the very near on our doorstep New Yea
 r 2025.\n\nThis walk is for all fitness levels. Please dress for the weath
 er and bring water. This tour begins on Queen Street East just west of Boo
 th Avenue adjacent to the Jimmie Simpson Recreation Centre at 870 Queen St
 reet East. We end at Leslie Street and Queen Street East!\n\nThis tour has
  a ticket price of $15.00 per person.\n\n\\*\\* **Please note: Please e-tr
 ansfer the ticket price when booking your space for this tour! You can e-t
 ransfer to the following email at:**\n**torontohistorywalks@gmail.com**
URL;VALUE=URI:https://www.meetup.com/the-history-of-parkdale/events/314890
 300/
STATUS:CONFIRMED
CREATED:20260521T122445Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260521T122445Z
CLASS:PUBLIC
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:Meetup: History of Parkdale
UID:event_314995548@meetup.com
SEQUENCE:1
DTSTAMP:20260621T050056Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260712T120000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260712T140000
SUMMARY:The People\, Places and Stories of Cabbagetown!
DESCRIPTION:Toronto History Walks\n\\*\\***The Toronto History Walks Yearl
 y Pass is available. Get it now for $125.00 for 1 year of unlimited tours\
 , email**\n**torontohistorywalks@gmail.com**\n**for more information or fo
 r signing up!\\*\\***\n\n\\*\\* **Please note: Please e-transfer the ticke
 t price when booking your space for this tour! You can e-transfer to the f
 ollowing email at:**\n**torontohistorywalks@gmail.com**\n\n**This walking 
 tour explores the fascinating history of Cabbagetown\, and the residents w
 ho contributed to the history\, the arts and sciences and literature of on
 e of Toronto's best known and beloved districts. It is different from the 
 History of Cabbagetown that I run every few months. This could be consider
 ed part two!**\n\nHave you ever wondered what life was like in Toronto at 
 the turn of the 20th century when the city was on the edge of becoming mod
 ern? A city with its face turned to the future but holding onto the romant
 ic ideas of the industrial revolution and the Victorian age.\n\nTake a ste
 p back in time to a world very different from our own\, a world of open-ai
 r streetcars and horse and buggy\, romantic notions\, and quaint and quiet
  days\, and boring Sundays. Welcome to the 19th century.\n\nWith two histo
 ric cemeteries and the Don Valley for inspiration\, this walking tour draw
 s on the beauty of the area and outlines some of the important historical 
 sites and will be of interest to anyone who loves domestic Victorian archi
 tecture.\n\nThis tour begins at the Toronto Public Library Parliament Bran
 ch at 269 Gerrard Street East just west of Parliament Street and continues
  northwards through the Don Vale and the necropolis cemetery on Winchester
  street. The tour ends a block north of the Winchester Hotel on Parliament
  Street and Wellesley.\n\nThis tour is designed for all walkers and weathe
 r conditions. Hope to see you soon.\n\nThis tour has a ticket price of $15
 .00 per person!\n\n\\*\\* **Please note: Please e-transfer the ticket pric
 e when booking your space for this tour! You can e-transfer to the followi
 ng email at:**\n**torontohistorywalks@gmail.com**
URL;VALUE=URI:https://www.meetup.com/the-history-of-parkdale/events/314995
 548/
STATUS:CONFIRMED
CREATED:20260528T151320Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260528T151320Z
CLASS:PUBLIC
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:Meetup: History of Parkdale
UID:event_315282642@meetup.com
SEQUENCE:1
DTSTAMP:20260621T050056Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260713T120000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260713T140000
SUMMARY:The History and Geology of the Scarborough Bluffs! (WEEKDAY)
DESCRIPTION:Toronto History Walks\n\\*\\***The Toronto History Walks Yearl
 y Pass is available. Get it now for $125.00 for 1 year of unlimited tours\
 , email**\n**torontohistorywalks@gmail.com**\n**for more information or fo
 r signing up!\\*\\***\n\n\\*\\* **Please note: Please e-transfer the ticke
 t amount when booking your space for this tour! You can e-transfer to the 
 following email at:**\n**torontohistorywalks@gmail.com**\n\nWelcome to Tor
 onto History Walks! This walking tour blends the human history and the nat
 ural history of the area. A fascinating tour\, so don't miss it. If you ar
 e new to Toronto then this tour is for you!\n\nThe Scarborough Bluffs is T
 oronto's best kept secret. Known as "Les Grands Ecores." by the French\, a
 nd in 1788 Alexander Aitken\, called the bluffs the High Lands. A hidden g
 em in Toronto which hides many secrets.\n\nElizabeth Simcoe named the Bluf
 fs the Scarborough Highlands in 1793 and had reminded Elizabeth Simcoe of 
 the limestone cliffs back in England\, in her own words from her diary:\n\
 n"The shore is extremely bold and has the appearance of chalk cliffs\, but
  I believe they are only white sand. They appeared so well that we talked 
 of building a summer residence there and calling it Scarborough."\n\nThe S
 carborough Bluffs extended west along the coastline of Lake Ontario toward
 s the town of York and later Toronto\, but vast areas along the western ed
 ge were razed for industrial and residential development. The formation of
  the chalk cliffs continues to shrink due to erosion.\n\nThe price of this
  tour is $15.00 per person\n\nThis extensive walking tour begins at Bluffe
 rs Park Road and Brimley Road South\, south of Kingston Road near the lake
  at the marina stop!\n\nThe 201 Bluffers Park Bus leaves Kennedy Subway St
 ation every 15 minutes.\n\nHope to see you there!\n\n\\*\\* **Please note:
  Please e-transfer the ticket amount when booking your space for this tour
 ! You can e-transfer to the following email at:**\n**torontohistorywalks@g
 mail.com**
URL;VALUE=URI:https://www.meetup.com/the-history-of-parkdale/events/315282
 642/
STATUS:CONFIRMED
CREATED:20260616T120632Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260616T120632Z
CLASS:PUBLIC
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:Meetup: History of Parkdale
UID:event_315230443@meetup.com
SEQUENCE:1
DTSTAMP:20260621T050056Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260717T123000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260717T143000
SUMMARY:City Architecture: The Annex\, Casa Loma and Spadina House!
DESCRIPTION:Toronto History Walks\n**The Toronto History Walks Yearly Pass
  is available. Get it now for $125.00 for 1 year of unlimited tours\, emai
 l**\n[torontohistorywalks@gmail.com](http://torontohistorywalks@gmail.com%
 2A%2A/)\n**for more information or for signing up!\\*\\***\n\n\\*\\* **Ple
 ase note: Please e-transfer the ticket amount when booking your space for 
 this tour! You can e-transfer to the following email at:**\n[torontohistor
 ywalks@gmail.com](http://torontohistorywalks@gmail.com%2A%2A/)\n\nGeorgian
 \, Gothic Revival\, Bay and Gable\, the list goes on and on. Toronto has m
 any styles\, and one can explore the history of Toronto simply by learning
  the different time periods involved.\n\nThis tour explores the **architec
 ture** of the Annex District\, **Casa Loma** and its grand competitor Spad
 ina House. These legendary landmarks on the hill overlooking the city have
  been focal points of Toronto history for well over a century in an area t
 hat has a vast story to tell.\n\nJust a reminder that we will be walking u
 p to the Case Loma site and exploring the grounds and the history\, we are
  not going inside any of the buildings.\n\nWe begin this walk in front of 
 the main doors to the Toronto Public Library Spadina Branch at 10 Spadina 
 Road. We end at St. Clair Avenue West at the Loblaws Superstore at the St.
  Clair West Subway Station. Hope to see you soon.\n\nThis walk is for most
  walking levels\; however\, there are steps and stairs near Casa Loma\, no
 rth of Davenport. Please dress for the weather and see you there.\n\nThe p
 rice of this tour is $15.00 per person!\n\n**Please note: Please e-transfe
 r the ticket amount when booking your space for this tour! You can e-trans
 fer to the following email at:**\n[torontohistorywalks@gmail.com](http://t
